<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Test Requirement Form — {{docNo}}</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/base.css">
<style>
  /* ── Whose document this is ──────────────────────────────────────────────
     Every other kf template opens with the Kashaya Fabs masthead, because every other kf
     document is OURS — we issue it. This one is not. The Test Requirement Form belongs to
     Lifestyle International (Easy Buy) and is submitted to Intertek; Kashaya Fabs is only
     the applicant filling it in, and appears in the "Applicant Name & Billing Information"
     and "Manufacturer's Name" fields exactly as on the buyer's original. So this template
     deliberately does NOT use the {{> mast}} partial — printing our letterhead on a lab's
     intake form would misattribute the document.

     Layout follows the buyer's own file field for field, in their order, as a bordered
     4-column table (label | value | label | value). That is not decoration: Intertek reads
     hundreds of these from different vendors and matches them against their own master, so
     a sheet that reflows the fields into a nicer grid is a sheet their intake desk has to
     re-read. Ours should look like the one they already know.

     Assets all come from the buyer's own .docx (word/media/): the Easy Buy mark was an EMF
     and has been rasterised; the Intertek mark and the Terms & Conditions page are their
     originals, unmodified. */

  .trf-mast{display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:space-between; gap:16px;
            padding-bottom:7px;}
  .trf-mast img.eb{height:26px; width:auto; flex:none;}
  .trf-mast img.itk{height:24px; width:auto; flex:none;}
  .trf-mast .who{text-align:center; flex:1;}
  .trf-mast .who .buyer{font-size:11.5px; font-weight:600;}
  .trf-mast .who h1{margin:2px 0 0; font-size:11px; letter-spacing:2.2px;
                    text-transform:uppercase; font-weight:600;}
  .trf-mast .who .docno{font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace; font-size:10px;
                        font-weight:600; color:var(--ink-2); margin-top:1px;}

  /* The form table. Thin rules on every cell, as the buyer's. base.css tables are
     bottom-ruled only — right for a statement, wrong for a form. */
  table.form{width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; table-layout:fixed;
             border:1px solid var(--rule-hard); font-size:9px;}
  table.form td{border:1px solid var(--rule); padding:2px 5px; vertical-align:top;
                line-height:1.35; word-break:break-word;}
  table.form td.k{background:var(--wash); font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;
                  font-size:7.5px; letter-spacing:.3px; text-transform:uppercase;
                  color:var(--ink-2); white-space:normal;}
  table.form td.v{font-weight:500;}
  table.form td.band{background:var(--wash); font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;
                     font-size:7.5px; letter-spacing:1.2px; text-transform:uppercase;
                     color:var(--ink-2); text-align:center;}
  /* A value we do not hold: hatched, for hand-fill. Never an em-dash — on a lab form that
     would read as "not applicable", which is a different claim from "not recorded". */
  td.v.hand{background:repeating-linear-gradient(45deg,transparent,transparent 5px,
            rgba(0,0,0,.05) 5px,rgba(0,0,0,.05) 10px);}
  td.office{background:repeating-linear-gradient(45deg,transparent,transparent 5px,
            rgba(0,0,0,.05) 5px,rgba(0,0,0,.05) 10px);}

  /* The TICK. No kf document has ever had a checkbox, because a kf document is a statement.
     A buyer's TRF is a form — ~60 boxes a lab reads. Two rules keep it inside the system:
     ticks are SYSTEM-populated so they are never hatched (base.css reserves the hatch for
     hand-fill, and inverting that breaks the one convention the design system turns on);
     and no new colour — the tick is --ink on --paper. */
  .tick{display:inline-block; width:7px; height:7px; margin-right:3px; flex:none;
        border:1px solid var(--rule-hard); background:var(--paper); vertical-align:-1px;}
  .tick.on{background:var(--ink); box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1.5px var(--paper);}
  .opts{display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:0 12px;}
  .opts span{display:inline-flex; align-items:center; white-space:nowrap;}
  .yn{display:inline-flex; gap:10px; white-space:nowrap;}
  .yn span{display:inline-flex; align-items:center;}

  /* The three printed columns of the buyer's sub-grid and test grid. */
  .cols3{display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr); column-gap:10px;}
  .cols3 .col{display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:0;}
  .cols3 .col > span{display:flex; align-items:flex-start; line-height:1.35;}
  .cols3 .col > span .tick{margin-top:1.5px;}

  .lab-foot{margin-top:6px; font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace; font-size:7px;
            line-height:1.5; letter-spacing:.3px; color:var(--ink-2); text-align:center;}
  .note{font-size:7.5px; color:var(--ink-2); font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;
        margin-top:4px; line-height:1.45;}

  /* Page 2 — Intertek's Terms and Conditions of Business, their artwork unaltered.
     The scan is 1100x1796, i.e. taller than A4's proportions: at full width it would be
     310mm against the 277mm the page allows, and spill onto a third sheet. So it is bounded
     by HEIGHT and centred, which keeps all 17 clauses on one page and legible. */
  .terms-sheet{display:flex; align-items:flex-start; justify-content:center;}
  .terms-sheet img{display:block; width:auto; height:auto;
                   max-width:100%; max-height:276mm; break-inside:avoid;}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<!-- ══════════════ PAGE 1 — the form ══════════════ -->
<div class="sheet">

  <div class="trf-mast">
    <img class="eb" src="assets/easybuy-logo.png" alt="Easy Buy">
    <div class="who">
      <div class="buyer">Lifestyle International Pvt Ltd &mdash; Easy Buy</div>
      <h1>Test Requirement Form</h1>
      <div class="docno">{{docNo}} &middot; {{trfDate}}</div>
    </div>
    <img class="itk" src="assets/intertek-logo.jpg" alt="Intertek">
  </div>

  <table class="form">
    <colgroup><col style="width:19%"><col style="width:31%"><col style="width:19%"><col style="width:31%"></colgroup>

    <tr>
      <td class="k">{{f.applicantName.label}}</td>
      <td class="v{{#if f.applicantName.hand}} hand{{/if}}">{{f.applicantName.value}}</td>
      <td class="k">Office Use Only:</td>
      <td class="office" rowspan="2"></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="k">{{f.address.label}}</td>
      <td class="v{{#if f.address.hand}} hand{{/if}}" colspan="2">{{f.address.value}}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="k">{{f.contactName.label}}</td>
      <td class="v{{#if f.contactName.hand}} hand{{/if}}">{{f.contactName.value}}</td>
      <td class="k">{{f.tel.label}}</td>
      <td class="v{{#if f.tel.hand}} hand{{/if}}">{{f.tel.value}}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="k">{{f.email.label}}</td>
      <td class="v{{#if f.email.hand}} hand{{/if}}" colspan="3">{{f.email.value}}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="k" rowspan="2">Easy Buy Merchandise:</td>
      <td class="k" style="background:transparent">Name:</td>
      <td class="v{{#if f.merchandiserName.hand}} hand{{/if}}" colspan="2">{{f.merchandiserName.value}}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="k" style="background:transparent">E-Mail I&rsquo;d:</td>
      <td class="v{{#if f.merchandiserEmail.hand}} hand{{/if}}" colspan="2">{{f.merchandiserEmail.value}}</td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
      <td class="k">{{f.sampleDescription.label}}</td>
      <td class="v{{#if f.sampleDescription.hand}} hand{{/if}}">{{f.sampleDescription.value}}</td>
      <td class="k">{{f.boNumber.label}}</td>
      <td class="v{{#if f.boNumber.hand}} hand{{/if}}">{{f.boNumber.value}}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="k">{{f.styleNo.label}}</td>
      <td class="v{{#if f.styleNo.hand}} hand{{/if}}">{{f.styleNo.value}}</td>
      <td class="k">{{f.colour.label}}</td>
      <td class="v{{#if f.colour.hand}} hand{{/if}}">{{f.colour.value}}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="k">{{f.fibreContent.label}}</td>
      <td class="v{{#if f.fibreContent.hand}} hand{{/if}}">{{f.fibreContent.value}}</td>
      <td class="k">{{f.ageRangeCategory.label}}</td>
      <td class="v{{#if f.ageRangeCategory.hand}} hand{{/if}}">{{f.ageRangeCategory.value}}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="k">{{f.endUse.label}}</td>
      <td class="v{{#if f.endUse.hand}} hand{{/if}}">{{f.endUse.value}}</td>
      <td class="k">{{f.orderNumber.label}}</td>
      <td class="v{{#if f.orderNumber.hand}} hand{{/if}}">{{f.orderNumber.value}}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="k">{{f.fabricWeight.label}}</td>
      <td class="v{{#if f.fabricWeight.hand}} hand{{/if}}">{{f.fabricWeight.value}}</td>
      <td class="k">{{f.yarnCount.label}}</td>
      <td class="v{{#if f.yarnCount.hand}} hand{{/if}}">{{f.yarnCount.value}}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="k">{{f.season.label}}</td>
      <td class="v{{#if f.season.hand}} hand{{/if}}">{{f.season.value}}</td>
      <td class="k">{{f.construction.label}}</td>
      <td class="v{{#if f.construction.hand}} hand{{/if}}">{{f.construction.value}}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="k">{{f.manufacturerName.label}}</td>
      <td class="v{{#if f.manufacturerName.hand}} hand{{/if}}">{{f.manufacturerName.value}}</td>
      <td class="k">Sample Testing stage:</td>
      <td class="v"><span class="opts">{{#each stageTicks}}<span><i class="tick{{#if this.on}} on{{/if}}"></i>{{this.label}}</span>{{/each}}</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="k">{{f.brandName.label}}</td>
      <td class="v{{#if f.brandName.hand}} hand{{/if}}">{{f.brandName.value}}</td>
      <td class="k">{{f.fabricSupplierName.label}}</td>
      <td class="v{{#if f.fabricSupplierName.hand}} hand{{/if}}">{{f.fabricSupplierName.value}}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="k">{{f.dyeingHouse.label}}</td>
      <td class="v{{#if f.dyeingHouse.hand}} hand{{/if}}">{{f.dyeingHouse.value}}</td>
      <td class="k">{{f.vendorCode.label}}</td>
      <td class="v{{#if f.vendorCode.hand}} hand{{/if}}">{{f.vendorCode.value}}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="k">{{f.processingHouse.label}}</td>
      <td class="v{{#if f.processingHouse.hand}} hand{{/if}}">{{f.processingHouse.value}}</td>
      <td class="k">Contrast/Trim Fabric is used within Garment</td>
      <td class="v">
        <span class="yn">
          <span><i class="tick{{#if yn.contrast.yes}} on{{/if}}"></i>YES</span>
          <span><i class="tick{{#if yn.contrast.no}} on{{/if}}"></i>NO</span>
        </span>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="k">Style With Sets Packing Together with Different Color</td>
      <td class="v">
        <span class="yn">
          <span><i class="tick{{#if yn.sets.yes}} on{{/if}}"></i>YES</span>
          <span><i class="tick{{#if yn.sets.no}} on{{/if}}"></i>NO</span>
        </span>
      </td>
      <td class="k">{{f.washCareCode.label}}</td>
      <td class="v{{#if f.washCareCode.hand}} hand{{/if}}">{{f.washCareCode.value}}</td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
      <td class="k">Finish Type:</td>
      <td class="v" colspan="3"><span class="opts">{{#each finishTicks}}<span><i class="tick{{#if this.on}} on{{/if}}"></i>{{this.label}}</span>{{/each}}</span></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
      <td class="k">Buying Dept.:</td>
      <td class="v" colspan="3">
        <span class="opts" style="margin-bottom:2px">{{#each departmentTicks}}<span><i class="tick{{#if this.on}} on{{/if}}"></i>{{this.label}}</span>{{/each}}</span>
        <div class="cols3">
          {{#each subCategoryColumns}}
          <div class="col">{{#each this}}<span><i class="tick{{#if this.on}} on{{/if}}"></i>{{this.label}}</span>{{/each}}</div>
          {{/each}}
        </div>
      </td>
    </tr>

    <tr><td class="band" colspan="4">Packages</td></tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="v" colspan="4">
        <span class="opts">
          {{#each packageTicks}}<span><i class="tick{{#if this.on}} on{{/if}}"></i>{{this.label}}</span>{{/each}}
          <span>Previous Report No: {{#if previousReportNo}}<b style="margin-left:4px">{{previousReportNo}}</b>{{else}}<i style="display:inline-block; width:90px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule); margin-left:4px"></i>{{/if}}</span>
        </span>
      </td>
    </tr>

    <tr><td class="band" colspan="4">Individual Test</td></tr>
    <!-- One cell spanning the table, with the three printed columns as an even grid inside.
         Splitting them across the table's own 19/31/19/31 columns makes them unequal and
         wraps half the labels; the buyer prints three equal columns. -->
    <tr>
      <td class="v" colspan="4">
        <div class="cols3">
          {{#each testColumns}}
          <div class="col">{{#each this}}<span><i class="tick{{#if this.on}} on{{/if}}"></i>{{this.label}}</span>{{/each}}</div>
          {{/each}}
        </div>
      </td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
      <td class="k">Service Required:</td>
      <td class="v" colspan="3"><span class="opts">{{#each serviceTicks}}<span><i class="tick{{#if this.on}} on{{/if}}"></i>{{this.label}}</span>{{/each}}</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td class="k">Report Delivery Service:</td>
      <td class="v">
        <span class="yn">
          <span><i class="tick{{#if yn.report.yes}} on{{/if}}"></i>Yes</span>
          <span><i class="tick{{#if yn.report.no}} on{{/if}}"></i>No</span>
        </span>
      </td>
      <td class="k">Return Remained Sample:</td>
      <td class="v">
        <span class="yn">
          <span><i class="tick{{#if yn.return.yes}} on{{/if}}"></i>Yes</span>
          <span><i class="tick{{#if yn.return.no}} on{{/if}}"></i>No</span>
        </span>
      </td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  {{#if remarks}}<div class="note">Remarks: {{remarks}}</div>{{/if}}
  {{#if handFilled.length}}
  <div class="note">Hatched fields are to be completed by hand: {{#each handFilled}}{{this}}{{#unless @last}}; {{/unless}}{{/each}}</div>
  {{/if}}

  <div class="sign">
    <div>Submitted By</div>
    <div>Received By (Lab)</div>
    <div>Date</div>
  </div>

  <!-- Intertek's own footer, transcribed from the buyer's file. This is the lab's address,
       not ours — our details are the applicant block at the top of the table. -->
  <div class="lab-foot">
    Intertek India Pvt. Ltd. &middot; 17/F, Industrial Suburb, 2nd Stage Industrial Area, Yeshwanthpur, Bangalore &ndash; 560022<br>
    T: +91 &ndash; 80 4021 3700 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; F: +91 &ndash; 80 4021 3960 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; E: labtest.india@intertek.com
  </div>

</div>

<!-- ══════════════ PAGE 2 — Intertek's Terms and Conditions ══════════════
     Their artwork, reproduced unaltered, exactly as it appears in the buyer's file. Not
     retyped on purpose: these are contract terms, and a transcription error in a liability
     clause would be ours to answer for. -->
<div class="sheet terms-sheet">
  <img src="assets/intertek-terms.png" alt="Intertek Testing Services India Pvt. Limited — Terms and Conditions of Business">
</div>

</body>
</html>
